[7.049, "o", "RESEARCHER NOTES:\r\n- Standard delivery window: 2 hours. (kestrel_customer_service_policy.pdf, id: kestrel_customer_service_policy#0)\r\n- Late delivery refund policy: if delivery arrives more than 20 minutes after the end of its window, customer receives 50% of the delivery fee. (kestrel_customer_service_policy.pdf, id: kestrel_customer_service_policy#0)\r\n- Refunds are issued automatically within 5 business days. (kestrel_customer_service_policy.pdf, id: kestrel_customer_service_policy#0)\r\n- For this specific incident (41 minutes late), a late-delivery refund was applied. (kestrel_incident_review_q3_2026.pdf, id: kestrel_incident_review_q3_2026#0)\r\n- Likely cause in this case: weather-related delay due to a lightning strike, with the aircraft grounded and the 15/30 rule applied (delay occurred while waiting at a s\r\n\r\nWRITER:\r\nYou qualify for a late-delivery refund: 50% of the delivery fee, automatically issued within 5 business days. For this 41-minute delay, a late-delivery refund was applied. The likely cause was weather-related: a lightning strike grounded the aircraft, the 15/30 rule was used, and the package waited at a safe landing point before delivery. If you’d like, I can check the exact "]
[7.049, "o", "refund amount for your order.\r\n"]
